WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:06.300
So we get a lot of questions about 
being a mentor.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:09.580
What does it mean to be a mentor, will you be my mentor, will I be your mentor?

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:11.170
Things like that.

00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:13.949
Here's what I've learned about mentorship.

00:00:13.949 --> 00:00:16.200
Mentorship is not something you ask
somebody to do like,

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.910
"Will you be my friend?"

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:19.860
It doesn't work like that.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.920
When you find somebody you get along with
you share values, you share beliefs.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:24.430
You spend time with them, you get to know
them.

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:29.030
You develop trust, you're vulnerable with
them, you open up to them.

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:32.160
And you discover that you become friends,
it's what happens.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.640
You start off as simply acquaintances.

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:37.249
In my experience, mentorship is 
exactly the same.

00:00:37.249 --> 00:00:42.969
There were people who were much more experienced
than me who had wisdom that I didn't have

00:00:42.969 --> 00:00:45.840
and when I would call them, they would
take my calls.

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:50.390
And when I would ask them questions, they
would always take the time to give me answers.

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:53.979
And over the course of time, they became
my mentors.

00:00:53.979 --> 00:00:55.730
Like they became my friends.

00:00:55.730 --> 00:01:00.990
And I remember one time I was with one of
my mentors, Ron Bruder, an amazing guy,

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:02.540
and I was leaving his house and I put my arm around
him and I said,

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:03.900
"You know, I'm glad you're my mentor,"

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:05.732
and he looked at me and he said,

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:07.120
"I'm glad you're mine."

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:10.400
And it caught me completely off guard.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:13.740
True mentorship, like true friendship, is
not a one way street.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:16.370
It's not about one person only giving advice
to the other.

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:21.530
Both people are showing up to give and both
people are showing up to learn.

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:25.420
But you can't ask someone to be your mentor,
especially someone who's a total stranger,

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:28.310
knock on their door and say, "Will you be
my mentor?" if they don't know you

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:29.310
and you've never met them.

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:30.350
It's like friendship.

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:34.730
You cultivate a relationship and if that person
is always there for you and wants to see you

00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:39.750
thrive and succeed and believes in you,
then perhaps they will become your mentor,

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:40.250
like making a friend.

